'''Camp Amana''' ({{lang-bl|Campamento de Amana}}), officially the '''Camp Amana Naval Support Station''' ({{lang-bl|Estacion Navale Apoyio Campamento de Amana}}; '''ENACA''') is a [[w:Military base|military base]] operated by the [[Baliscan Navy]], located in [[Nacala]], [[Zambezi]]. It is the first overseas Baliscan military facility, and was built at a cost of {{USD|600 million}}. The base's presence was spearheaded as part of Baliscan social internationalism and has resulted in increased Baliscan investment in Nacala's development, including the revitalization of port facilities and the waterfront. The [[Baliscan Development Agency]] is heavily involved in social development programs such as education, medical and [[W:Reproductive care|reproductive care]] services, while the base and its logistical organs employ a substantial number of locals in support of the local economy. 

[[File:The bird's view of the harbour in Dar es Salaam.jpg|thumb|250px|left|Nacala's port has seen exensive growth since Balisca's involvement.]]

The construction of ENACA is a direct result of Baliscan efforts to cultivate closer relations with Sub-Saharan Africa and strengthen Baliscan [[w:Piracy in the 21st century|anti-piracy measures]] in the [[w:Indian Ocean|Indian Ocean]]. All Baliscan forces working under the [[w:Combined Task Force 150|Combined Task Force 150]] operate from ENACA. Camp Amana is the largest foreign military community in [[Zambezi]], housing [[Baliscan Navy|Confederal Navy]] personnel. There are also a handful of [[Baliscan Aerospace Force|Aerospace Force]] contingents on the base. In 2019, the Baliscan helicopter carrier ''[[VB Arruazu (CVH-183)]]'' visited the base on a [[w:Port#Port_of_call|port call]], and over it's weeklong visit, generated over five million dollars in economic activity. Joint research into the economic impact of ENACA determined that the personnel based a Camp Amana itself injected upwards of $800 million into the local economy annually, which increases substantially when taking into account visiting naval vessels.

===Waterfront revitalisation===
[[File:TPAHQ.jpg|thumb|250px|left|New developments along Nacala's waterfront.]]
Located in the southwestern indentation of inner Fernao Veloso Bay, the harbour is located in the deepest natural port on the east coast of Africa. 

Since the Port's construction and waterfront revitalisation, numerous hotels, residential apartments and commercial districts have sprung up around the area from increased national and local government investment. Controversy has arisen throughout the development due to the area initially being home to large areas of slums that were acquired by the government, forcfully relocating thousands of residents. Most residents in these slums had been relocated to other parts of the city, with new government housing established on the outskirts of the city. 

